      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T11:06:55Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): stock axis choice on the Stock page (along Z, X, Y or custom)\n\nThe Stock page sets the whole stock turn, not only a yaw. The turn is\nstored in the stock's Location.rot and lands through the undoable\nSetStock. The page reads a stored turn back, and it shows a plain note\nbefore a simulation when the simulation cannot cut the stock (a laid\ncylinder or a tilted stock). MCP set_stock takes an optional axis or\nangles_deg. A DXF profile lies on the real top face of a laid box, and a\nlaid cylinder or a tilted stock is refused by name.\n\nFixes #2576\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
